 "notes": {
  "ISL": "The Icelandic fidla is a bowed box zither, so I coded it as bowzither along with the langspil; I did not count the violin as a separate folk tradition. Organ = harmonium and the Lutheran church organ.",
  "NOR": "Hardingfele/fiddle, psalmodikon, langeleik, seljefloyte, Meraker clarinet, lur/bukkehorn, munnharpe.",
  "SWE": "Nyckelharpa counted as bowed lute; vevlira = hurdy; hummel. The folk clarinet (Halsingland) and the revived sackpipa were judgement calls.",
  "FIN": "Jouhikko, kantele, virsikannel. Brass is for the 19th-c village brass septet tradition. Bagpipe left out because it died out early.",
  "DEN": "The spillemand ensemble (fiddle, clarinet, accordion) and the humle. Bronze lurs are ancient finds, so not counted.",
  "EST": "Hiiukannel/talharpa, kannel, roopill, torupill, sarv, lootspill, parmupill.",
  "LAT": "Kokle, stabule (counted as both flute and reed), dudas, taure, trideksnis, bungas; cimbole from Latgale.",
  "LIT": "Kankles, skuduciai, lumzdelis, birbyne, ragas/trimitas, dudmaisis, cimbolai, bandonion in the village kapela.",
  "RUS": "Gudok, balalaika/domra, the seven-string guitar (urban folk), gusli, svirel/kugikly, zhaleika, rozhok, garmon/bayan, lozhki, zvon bells. The volynka is rare. No organ (Orthodox).",
  "BLR": "Lira, gusli, tsymbaly, dudka, zhaleika, duda, buben. Organ excluded because the majority is Orthodox.",
  "POL": "Suka/zlobcoki, lira korbowa, cymbaly, dwojnice, koza/dudy, trombita/ligawka, burczybas, diabelskie skrzypce. The harmonia pedalowa is counted under both accordion and organ.",
  "IRL": "Irish bouzouki, plus guitar and banjo in trad sessions (banjo coded under longneck); the piano and drums of the ceili band; bodhran, bones and spoons.",
  "ULS": "As for IRL, plus the Lambeg drum and the flute/fife, accordion and silver bands of the marching-band tradition.",
  "SCO": "Clarsach, pipes and pipe-band drums, and the Scottish dance band (accordion, piano, drums). Bouzouki and guitar are modern trad. Organ is liturgical (adopted late).",
  "ENG": "Welsh crwth, triple harp and pibgorn; Northumbrian pipes; pipe and tabor; colliery brass bands; melodeon/concertina; change ringing and morris bells; East Anglian dulcimer; west gallery and barrel organs.",
  "NLD": "Hommel, doedelzak, midwinterhoorn, street organ, rommelpot, carillon, fanfare bands.",
