  "GRE": "Lyra, violi, laouto/bouzouki, oud/mandolin, kanonaki, santouri, floghera, klarino, zournas, tsabouna/gaida, defi, daouli, toumbeleki, koutalia, carnival kudounia.",
  "USA": "Anglo- and African-American: fiddle, banjo (coded longneck), guitar/mandolin, autoharp and Appalachian dulcimer, washtub bass, hammered dulcimer, blues/gospel piano, fife and drum, quills, Cajun accordion, harmonica, gospel tambourine, washboard/bones/spoons, jaw harp, New Orleans brass bands. Sax and electric left out because I treated jazz and R&B as popular genres. No indigenous instruments.",
  "CAN": "Cape Breton and Ottawa Valley fiddle with piano and guitar, Newfoundland accordion/concertina, Highland pipes, spoons. No indigenous instruments.",
